                <pb facs="0694" n="610" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg610"/>

                <p rendition="#center">[Seal: Office, Political Chief of Canton Degollado.]</p>
                <p>By a swift messenger sent to-day I state to the political chief, district of
                    Guerrero, the following: “From two letters addressed to Mr. Santana Perez, it is
                    known to this office that on the 17th instant the Apaches murdered, near the
                    Cerro de los Borregos (Sheep Mountain) a person named Luis Soto, that there are
                    15 of the Apaches; and that on the 18th instant they murdered at Las Varas two
                    Americans. I communicate this to you, that you may report these facts, in the
                    most expeditious way to the executive of the State.” I send you a copy of the
                    foregoing for the executive itself.</p>
                <p>Liberty and constitution.</p>
                <p>Temosachic, October 20, 1885.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">To the secretary of the supreme government of the State,
                        Chihuahua.</hi></p>
            </div>
